Subject: [M156] [ganesh] Handle negative determinants in StrokeIterator for
 hairline square caps

Original change's description:
> [ganesh] Handle negative determinants in StrokeIterator for hairline square caps
>
> A negative determinant is perfectly valid, e.g. from a negative Y scale.
> Without this fix, the outset to form a square cap on zero-length
> lines would be length 1 in local space, but the negative Y scale could
> scale this square arbitrarily large.
>
> Using |det| could work, but would result in flipping the square
> (not visually noticeable). Instead I opted to just always apply the
> inverse determinant and then check for finiteness afterwards to
> handle scenarios where the outset itself overflows when det was a
> subnormal value.
>
